      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "FREMARKS PEGGY (2) produced a better performance at her latest appearance when second at Maryborough, beaten 1.5 metres. Returns to a mobile start but a low draw on the front line should ensure a cosy run. Can win with her A-game. QUEEN KIZEN NZ (6) came from a 20m handicap and worked last start so it may pay to overlook that result. She was good in scoring at the previous appearance at Globe Derby so with even luck from a wide draw she is capable of a strong performance. SCAR (5) raced parked from this barrier but boxed on to go under by 3.7m last week. Recorded a string of wins and placings prior. Contender. ASPEN BELLE (3) has been trialling well since breaking last start. Overcame tougher draws than this to win two in a row prior. Chance with manners.",
